render_lab's story library for Lamlet
=====================================

A storyboard is a Lamlet presentation (`storyboard.lam`, tools/video/README.md), and imports this package with
`$$[Import* render_lab]`. Its cues are `present`'s `cue` and `during`, with attributes from the investigation's
vocabulary (`render-lab story keys`, generated by the video builder) and from here: the attributes whose values
have a shape of their own (motions, points, marks, lists of names, records, formulas), typed, so a wrong one is a
type error at the storyboard's line. Each writes the String the lab reads (tools/video/markup.py). Its other
functions compute narration: numbers spoken as words, so the voice reads them right. Nothing here runs at
playback.

$[Import* std]$[Import* content]$[Import* present]$[Import rl]

Numbers as the voice says them

Narration says its numbers in words, so the voice reads them right: `spoken` writes a non-negative Int in
English words, `spokenFloat` a Float with its decimals ("three point two"), `rounded` an Int to its leading
`digits` significant digits ("about forty-two thousand" is `rounded 42289 2`).

$[# _ones [% {' "zero" "one" "two" "three" "four" "five" "six" "seven" "eight" "nine" "ten" "eleven" "twelve"
                "thirteen" "fourteen" "fifteen" "sixteen" "seventeen" "eighteen" "nineteen"}]]
$[# _tens [% {' "" "" "twenty" "thirty" "forty" "fifty" "sixty" "seventy" "eighty" "ninety"}]]
$[# {_under100 n} {!if {< n 20} {nth _ones n}
        {!if {= {% n 10} 0} {nth _tens {div n 10}}
            {++ {nth _tens {div n 10}} {++ "-" {nth _ones {% n 10}}}}}}]
$[# {_under1000 n} {!if {< n 100} {_under100 n}
        {!if {= {% n 100} 0}
            {++ {nth _ones {div n 100}} " hundred"}
            {++ {nth _ones {div n 100}} {++ " hundred " {_under100 {% n 100}}}}}}]
$[# {_withScale self n unit name} [# r {% n unit}]
    {++ {self {div n unit}} {++ " " {++ name {!if {= r 0} "" {++ " " {self r}}}}}}]
$[# {spoken n}
    {!if {< n 0} {++ "minus " {spoken {neg n}}}
        {!if {< n 1000} {_under1000 n}
            {!if {< n 1000000} {_withScale spoken n 1000 "thousand"}
                {!if {< n 1000000000} {_withScale spoken n 1000000 "million"}
                    {_withScale spoken n 1000000000 "billion"}}}}}]
$[# {_digit c} {withDefault {fold {range 0 10} none {^ {found d} {!if {= {str d} c} {some d} found}}} 0}]
$[# {_digitWords digits} {join " " {map {chars digits} {^ {c} {nth _ones {_digit c}}}}}]
$[# {_toInt digits} {fold {chars digits} 0 {^ {acc c} {+ {* acc 10} {_digit c}}}}]
$[# {spokenFloat x} [# text {str {abs x}}]
    [# parts {split text "."}]
    [# whole {spoken {_toInt {head parts}}}]
    [# sign {!if {< x 0.0} "minus " ""}]
    {!if {= {length parts} 1}
        {++ sign whole}
        {!if {= {nth parts 1} "0"}
            {++ sign whole}
            {++ sign {++ whole {++ " point " {_digitWords {nth parts 1}}}}}}}]
$[# {_pow10 k} {!if {<= k 0} 1 {* 10 {_pow10 {- k 1}}}}]
$[# {rounded n digits} [# size {length {chars {str {abs n}}}}]
    [# step {_pow10 {- size digits}}]
    [# r {* {div {+ {abs n} {div step 2}} step} step}]
    {spoken {!if {< n 0} {neg r} r}}]

A sentence's first word with its first letter capitalized: `{capitalized {spoken 42}}` is "Forty-two".

$[# _lower [% {chars "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz"}]]
$[# _upper [% {chars "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ"}]]
$[# {_capital c} {fold {range 0 26} c {^ {out i} {!if {= {nth _lower i} c} {nth _upper i} out}}}]
$[# {capitalized s} [# cs {chars s}]
    {!if {isEmpty cs} s {++ {_capital {head cs}} {concat {tail cs}}}}]

JSON, as the lab reads a motion

$[# {_quoted s} {++ "\"" {++ s "\""}}]
$[# {_array xs} {++ "[" {++ {join ", " xs} "]"}}]
$[# {_floats xs} {_array {map {: xs {List Float}} str}}]
$[# {_object fields} {++ "{" {++ {join ", " {map fields {^ {f} {++ {_quoted {.name f}} {++ ": " {.json f}}}}}} "}"}}]

Motions

A motion moves one or more channels of the shot over time (lab/src/animation.rs): a `path` through waypoints, an
`orbit` about a centre, or a `sway`, a sine wave about the channel's value. Its channels are the vocabulary's own
functions (`{path {' cameraYaw cameraPitch} …}`), so a misspelled channel is an unknown name and a channel that is
not a number (a vector, a choice) a type error. How long it runs is a `Length`: until the end of the cue's `beat`
or `sentence`, or `{seconds 4.0}`.

$[# Length [% {Variant {' {Field "beat" Unit} {Field "sentence" Unit} {Field "seconds" Float}}}]]
$[# beat [% {: {#beat unit} Length}]]
$[# sentence [% {: {#sentence unit} Length}]]
$[# {seconds s} {: {#seconds s} Length}]
$[# {_length l} {!case {: l Length} {beat u {_quoted "beat"}} {sentence u {_quoted "sentence"}} {seconds s {str s}}}]

A motion: its kind (`path`, `orbit`, or `wave`) and its fields as JSON, in order.

$[# _Field [% {Struct {' {Field "name" String} {Field "json" String}}}]]
$[# Motion [% {Struct {' {Field "kind" String} {Field "fields" {List _Field}}}}]]
$[# {_motion kind fields} {: {. kind kind fields fields} Motion}]
$[# {_field name json} {: {. name name json json} _Field}]
$[# {_channel f} {.key {: {f 0.0} Attr}}]
$[# {_channels fs} {_array {map fs {^ {f} {_quoted {_channel f}}}}}]
$[# {_count what fs xs} {!if {= {length fs} {length xs}} unit
    {error {++ what {++ " has one value per channel: " {++ {str {length fs}} {++ ", not " {str {length xs}}}}}}}}]

Through `waypoints` after the start (one value per channel each), on a smooth curve.

$[# {path channels waypoints length}
    [# checked {map waypoints {^ {w} {_count "a waypoint" channels w}}}]
    {_motion "path" {' {_field "params" {_channels channels}}
                       {_field "through" {_array {map waypoints _floats}}}
                       {_field "seconds" {_length length}}}}]

About `center` (one value per channel), by `degrees`: two channels turn in their plane, from the first towards
the second; three about an axis (`around`; up by default).

$[# {orbit channels center degrees length}
    [# checked {_count "an orbit's center" channels center}]
    {_motion "orbit" {' {_field "params" {_channels channels}}
                        {_field "center" {_floats center}}
                        {_field "degrees" {str {: degrees Float}}}
                        {_field "seconds" {_length length}}}}]

A sine wave of `amplitude` and `period` (seconds) about the channel's value when it starts, for ever unless
`lasting`.

$[# {sway channel amplitude period}
    {_motion "wave" {' {_field "param" {_quoted {_channel channel}}}
                       {_field "amplitude" {str {: amplitude Float}}}
                       {_field "period" {str {: period Float}}}}}]

A motion's optional parts, each a wrapper (only the kinds it names take it): the pace along it (`eased`, with the
vocabulary's easing, `easingSine`), going round again (`looping`, `pingPonging`), back to its start at the end (a
path, `closed`), the axis of a three-channel orbit (`around`), the point an orbit starts from (`from`), a wave's
centre (`centered`), its phase in degrees (`phased`), how long it waves (`lasting`), and the seconds over which its
amplitude grows and shrinks (`fading`).

$[# {_part kinds name json m}
    {!if {contains kinds {.kind m}} {.fields= m {append {.fields m} {' {_field name json}}}}
        {error {++ "a " {++ {.kind m} {++ " motion has no " name}}}}}]
$[# _easings [% {' "smooth" "linear" "in" "out" "inOut" "sine"}]]
$[# {_easeName easing} {fold _easings "" {^ {found n} {!if {= {.value {: easing Attr}} {toData n}} n found}}}]
$[# {eased easing m} {!if {= {.key {: easing Attr}} "ease"} {_part {' "path" "orbit"} "ease" {_quoted {_easeName easing}} m}
    {error {++ "eased takes an easing (easingSine, …), not " {.key easing}}}}]
$[# {looping m} {_part {' "path" "orbit"} "repeat" {_quoted "loop"} m}]
$[# {pingPonging m} {_part {' "path" "orbit"} "repeat" {_quoted "pingPong"} m}]
$[# {closed m} {_part {' "path"} "closed" "true" m}]
$[# {around axis m} {_part {' "orbit"} "axis" {_floats axis} m}]
$[# {from start m} {_part {' "orbit"} "start" {_floats start} m}]
$[# {centered center m} {_part {' "wave"} "center" {str {: center Float}} m}]
$[# {phased degrees m} {_part {' "wave"} "phase" {str {: degrees Float}} m}]
$[# {lasting length m} {_part {' "wave"} "seconds" {_length length} m}]
$[# {fading s m} {_part {' "wave"} "fade" {str {: s Float}} m}]

The cue attribute: the motions a key starts (`animate`).

$[# {motion motions} {attr "animate" {_array {map {: motions {List Motion}} {^ {m} {_object {' {_field {.kind m} {_object {.fields m}}}}}}}}}]

The camera's own paths, over the beat: `cameraPath` through yaw, pitch, and distance waypoints (`{' 18.0 16.0
6.2}`), `cameraTurn` through yaw and pitch.

$[# {_cameraYaw x} {attr "camera.yaw" {str {: x Float}}}]
$[# {_cameraPitch x} {attr "camera.pitch" {str {: x Float}}}]
$[# {_cameraDistance x} {attr "camera.distance" {str {: x Float}}}]
$[# {cameraPath waypoints} {path {' _cameraYaw _cameraPitch _cameraDistance} waypoints beat}]
$[# {cameraTurn waypoints} {path {' _cameraYaw _cameraPitch} waypoints beat}]

Ranges

A range needs a name only to be told from another: `over` and `overText` are `present`'s `during` and
`duringText` without one (tools/video/presentation.py names it).

$[# {over attrs body} {during "" attrs body}]
$[# {overText attrs s} {duringText "" attrs s}]

Another view's values

A cue sets the main view's values; `view` makes its attributes another view's (lab/src/view.rs): each named
`view.<name>.<key>`, a view an investigation stacks over the main one (its own camera keys too). It wraps a cue's
or a range's attributes (`cue "key" {view "field" {' {fieldMorph 1.0}}}`, or a range's `{view "field" {'
{fieldMorphRange 0.0 1.0}}}`), and joins other attributes with `append`.

$[# {view name attrs} {map {: attrs {List Attr}} {^ {a} {attr {++ "view." {++ name {++ "." {.key a}}}} {.value a}}}}]

Points, marks, and names

A point in the scene, for an arrow's ends and a label: three coordinates, or a point the package publishes
(`probe.top`).

$[# Point [% {Variant {' {Field "at" {List Float}} {Field "named" String}}}]]
$[# {at x y z} {: {#at {' x y z}} Point}]
$[# {point name} {: {#named {rl::point name}} Point}]
$[# {_point p} {!case {: p Point} {at xs {join "," {map {: xs {List Float}} str}}} {named n n}}]
$[# {labelAt p} {attr "labelAt" {_point p}}]
$[# {arrowFrom p} {attr "arrowFrom" {_point p}}]
$[# {arrowTo p} {attr "arrowTo" {_point p}}]

A region of an image to point out, in fractions of the picture (`u0 v0` to `u1 v1`), and its mark faded out.

$[# {mark u0 v0 u1 v1} {attr "imageMark" {join "," {map {: {' u0 v0 u1 v1} {List Float}} str}}}]
$[# unmark [% {attr "imageMark" ""}]]

Names to hide or to call out: images, arrows, labels, and the code panel's or the graph's highlighted lines and
passes. An empty list clears the highlight.

$[# {_name n} {!if {contains {chars n} ","} {error {++ "a name has no comma: " n}} n}]
$[# {_names key names} {attr key {join "," {map {: names {List String}} _name}}}]
$[# {imageHide names} {_names "imageHide" names}]
$[# {arrowHide names} {_names "arrowHide" names}]
$[# {labelHide names} {_names "labelHide" names}]
$[# {highlight names} {_names "highlight" names}]

What the frame records (`record`): nothing, the camera, or one object (by index).

$[# recordNone [% {attr "record" "none"}]]
$[# recordCamera [% {attr "record" "camera"}]]
$[# {recordObject index} {attr "record" {++ "object:" {str {: index Int}}}}]

Names the lab checks

A callout (a key of the investigation's source index), and the text keys an image's title, its mark's label, and
a label show (keys of the package's text table, or the lab's), each checked by the lab (`rl`, its natives) at the
storyboard's line; an empty one clears it.

$[# {_checked key check name} {attr key {!if {= name ""} "" {check name}}}]
$[# {callout name} {_checked "callout" rl::source name}]
$[# {imageTitle name} {_checked "imageTitle" rl::text name}]
$[# {imageMarkText name} {_checked "imageMarkText" rl::text name}]
$[# {labelText name} {_checked "labelText" rl::text name}]

A range whose words start with a callout: the source-index entry `key` is shown as the range's words begin.

$[# {overCallout attrs key words} {during "" attrs {cat {' {text " "} {cue "key" {' {callout key}}} {text {++ " " words}}}}}]

Formulas

A formula, and what the voice says for it: the formula card's cue (with `attrs` besides the LaTeX: `colors`,
`term`, `display`, `card`) and the `say` that shows it, from one LaTeX String, which the lab typesets first.

$[# {formulaSaid tex said attrs} {cat {' {anchor "formula" {cons {attr "formula" {rl::formula tex}} attrs}} {say {math tex} said}}}]
